00009| const GUIDE_MD = `# NEXUS field guide
00010| 
00011| NEXUS is an investigation workbench for **authorized-use OSINT**: you point it
00012| only at subjects and platforms you are permitted to inspect, and it keeps the
00013| receipts for everything it collects. This handbook covers both layers of the
00014| system and every surface of this UI. Reading time is about five minutes — and
00015| the walkthrough below really is that fast in practice.
00016| 
00017| ## NEXUS in one minute
00018| 
00019| Two layers, one pipeline:
00020| 
00021| - **The OSINT hub** (root app, port 8799) finds raw footprint. Give it a
00022|   username, phone number, email address or image URL and it fans out through
00023|   the toolchain — \`sherlock\` + \`maigret\` sweep a username across social
00024|   platforms, \`phoneinfoga\` + \`ignorant\` produce phone intel and
00025|   registration checks, \`holehe\` finds where an email is registered, and
00026|   \`revimg\` discovers pages where an image appears.
00027| - **NEXUS** (this workbench, port 8801) turns those findings into an evidence
00028|   graph. Every hit becomes an entity; entities get typed relations; every
00029|   claim carries provenance — which tool produced it, and the URL it came
00030|   from. On top of the graph you get wiki docs, dossiers, article briefs, and
00031|   a handoff path to archon for cited drafting.
00032| 
00033| Hub = collection. NEXUS = case file. Nothing is asserted without a source row
00034| behind it.
00035| 
00036| ## Your first investigation (5 minutes)
00037| 
00038| 1. **① New case** — in the left rail, type a name into the "new case name…"
00039|    field and press Enter. The case owns everything that follows.
00040| 2. **② Add a seed entity** — pick an etype in the add-entity form (defaults
00041|    to \`username\`) and give it a label, e.g. \`janedoe\`. The node appears in
00042|    the graph immediately.
00043| 3. **③ Hub scan** — click the node to open it in the inspector, find ACTIONS,
00044|    press "▶ hub scan". This runs the sherlock+maigret sweep via the hub, and
00045|    every hit is ingested automatically as entities + \`uses\` relations +
00046|    evidence rows carrying tool and URL provenance. No copy-pasting.
00047| 4. **④ Watch it live** — the console strip along the bottom lists tasks.
00048|    Click a row to expand its per-task SSE log stream while the sweep runs;
00049|    ingested counts land on the task row when it finishes.
00050| 5. **⑤ Read the graph** — back in the Graph tab, nodes are colored by type
00051|    (the chips above the graph are the color map and double as hide/show
00052|    filters). Shift-click two nodes to highlight the shortest connection path
00053|    between them; Esc clears it.
00054| 6. **⑥ Analyze** — the Analysis tab ranks PageRank centrality (who matters
00055|    in this graph), groups communities (clusters of closely related entities),
00056|    and deals pivot cards: next-best actions computed from the graph shape,
00057|    each runnable with one click.
00058| 7. **⑦ Write it up** — in the inspector, switch to WIKI DOC and hit render.
00059|    The skeleton auto-fills the Connections / Timeline / Sources sections from
00060|    the graph; your prose under Summary and Open questions is preserved on
00061|    every regeneration.
00062| 8. **⑧ Draft for publication** — the Story tab renders Dossier.md (findings
00063|    with an evidence appendix) and an article brief: lede angles, a nut graf,
00064|    a claim ledger where every claim is tagged Supported / Single-source /
00065|    Unverified, and the source list behind them.
00066| 9. **⑨ Hand off** — "⇪ push case to archon" seeds a canon sandbox with the
00067|    case, so drafting in archon stays grounded in this evidence, citations
00068|    included.
00069| 
00070| ## Connectors
00071| 
00072| Connectors are the server's outboards; their health shows as dots in the left
00073| rail. \`up\` is green. \`down\` means configured but unreachable (red) — its
00074| tasks fail fast with a clear error while everything else keeps working.
00075| \`unset\` means not configured (gray): the connector's actions simply are not
00076| offered. Degradation is graceful by design.
00077| 
00078| | connector | what it does | needs |
00079| | --- | --- | --- |
00080| | hub | username / phone / email / image scans via the qalarc OSINT hub (sherlock, maigret, phoneinfoga, ignorant, holehe, revimg) | hub_url, optional hub_token |
00081| | flowsint | subdomain, WHOIS, ASN, breach and crypto enrichers | flowsint_url pointing at a running flowsint instance |
00082| | openplanter | recursive AI agent deep-dives seeded from a node | openplanter-agent binary on PATH |
00083| | archon | canon / RAG grounding — evidence push, cited answers | archon_url |
00084| | laya | local fine-tuned decision model for lead triage | laya_url (empty = heuristic) |
00085| | jev | TypeSafe calibrated decision engine (remote) | jev_url + jev_api_key |
00086| 
00087| Set FLOWSINT_URL (or the matching Settings field) to a running flowsint
00088| instance to enable its enrichers; openplanter needs the agent binary
00089| discoverable on PATH unless you set the path explicitly in Settings.
00090| 
00091| ## Calibrated decisions (jev → laya → heuristic)
00092| 
00093| Where the workbench has to rank things — chiefly lead triage in Analysis —
00094| it walks a fixed chain and takes the first link that answers:
00095| 
00096| 1. **jev** — remote and calibrated. Set jev_url and jev_api_key in Settings
00097|    and it works instantly, returning probabilities with honest confidence.
00098| 2. **laya** — local and trainable. Every decision it serves is appended to
00099|    laya-decisions.jsonl, so you can fine-tune the model on your own verdicts
00100|    and redeploy it.
00101| 3. **heuristic** — a graph-shaped fallback (centrality, degree, recency).
00102|    Never configured, never down.
00103| 
00104| ### The merge gate
00105| 
00106| The inspector's merge flow offers candidate duplicates for an entity.
00107| Confirming one runs a same-entity check (jaro-winkler similarity on labels):
00108| **≥ 0.8** produces an auto-merge offer, **0.5–0.8** is flagged for human
00109| review, and **< 0.5** is treated as distinct. A confirmed merge re-points
00110| relations, keeps a \`same_as\` edge, and writes an audit entry — nothing is
00111| silently rewritten.
00112| 
00113| ## Tabs reference
00114| 
00115| - **Graph** — the evidence map. Nodes colored by etype (chips are legend and
00116|   filters), label search, force / grid / circle layouts, fit view.
00117|   Shift-click two nodes for the shortest connection path.
00118| - **Console** — task queue with status, ingested entity / relation / evidence
00119|   counts, and expandable per-task SSE logs (the last 500 lines are kept).
00120| - **Timeline** — case chronology. Ingested milestones land here; add manual
00121|   events with a kind, title, optional entity link and source.
00122| - **Analysis** — PageRank centrality table, communities, pivot cards,
00123|   laya-ranked leads.
00124| - **Story** — Dossier.md and the article brief, with copy / download buttons
00125|   and push-to-archon.
00126| 
00127| ## Desktop & hosting
00128| 
00129| - **Desktop app (Tauri)** — from the repository's \`nexus/\` directory:
00130|   \`cargo run -p nexus-tauri --features desktop\`.
00131| - **Server-only** — \`scripts/run_nexus.sh\` builds and serves UI + API on
00132|   \`127.0.0.1:8801\`.
00133| - **Hosting tiers** — localhost is tier zero. For a shareable URL, a quick
00134|   tunnel: \`cloudflared tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:8801\`. For a stable
00135|   subdomain, run a named cloudflared tunnel and put Cloudflare Access in
00136|   front of it. For a static showcase, host the built UI anywhere and point it
00137|   at the server with the API-base override: open the page once with
00138|   \`?api=<server-url>\` or set nexus_api_base in Settings. The server must
00139|   allow the UI's origin in its CORS config for a cross-origin showcase to
00140|   connect. If the server runs
00141|   with NEXUS_TOKEN set, put that token in nexus_token (Settings) and every
00142|   request — API and SSE alike — carries it as a bearer header.
00143| 
00144| ## Settings & keys
00145| 
00146| The gear icon (top right) opens the settings modal. Connector fields are
00147| stored in this browser (localStorage \`nexus_settings\`) **and** applied to
00148| the server via POST /api/admin/config; environment variables remain the
00149| defaults and empty fields are sent as null. Secrets are redacted in responses
00150| — you only ever see whether they are set. The two connection fields stay in
00151| this browser only.
00152| 
00153| | field | what it does |
00154| | --- | --- |
00155| | hub_url | OSINT hub endpoint (default 127.0.0.1:8799) |
00156| | hub_token | bearer token if the hub requires one |
00157| | flowsint_url | flowsint enrichers endpoint; unset disables them |
00158| | openplanter_bin | openplanter-agent binary (auto-discovered on PATH) |
00159| | archon_url | archon canon / RAG endpoint |
00160| | laya_url | local laya decision server; empty = heuristic only |
00161| | jev_url | TypeSafe decision engine endpoint |
00162| | jev_api_key | TypeSafe API key — enables calibrated jev decisions |
00163| | nexus_api_base | browser-only: where this UI finds the API (empty = same-origin) |
00164| | nexus_token | browser-only: bearer token for NEXUS_TOKEN-gated servers |
00165| 
00166| /api/health stays open even when the token gate is on, so the rail can show
00167| connector state without credentials.
00168| 
00169| ## Ethics & privacy
00170| 
00171| This is a tool for **authorized-use OSINT**: investigate subjects you have
00172| the right and the mandate to investigate — your own footprint, consented
00173| research, or engagements with a written scope. Results are investigative
00174| leads with provenance, not proof; that is exactly why the claim ledger exists
00175| with Supported / Single-source / Unverified statuses, so journalism stays
00176| honest about what any one source supports. Only public footprint is
00177| collected, and only on request. Respect platform terms and local law. The
00178| full data-handling statement lives in PRIVACY.md at the repository root.
00179| `;
